            "category": "Implementation & Deployment",
            "question": "How long does implementation take from contract to go-live?",
            "answer": "Typical timeline is 4-6 weeks for a single store, 8-12 weeks for multi-store rollouts. Week 1-2: Infrastructure assessment and camera placement planning. Week 3-4: Hardware installation and network integration. Week 5-6: Calibration, validation, and staff training. For enterprise deployments (10+ stores), we follow a phased rollout: pilot store first (6 weeks), then standardized deployment at 2-3 stores per week. Timeline assumes existing network infrastructure meets requirements (PoE-capable switches, 100Mbps per camera). If network upgrades are needed, add 2-4 weeks for infrastructure work.",
